// @probe: unit-as-main-result
// @capability: `myc run` executing a main whose result is a data/ADT value (here Unit)
// @expect-check: 0
// @expect-run: 65
// @claim: EXPRESSIBILITY-GAPS s3.1 bullet 1: "No unit value ()" (l1#6) — MISLEADING as phrased
// @note: `Unit` DOES exist (PRELUDE_UNCONDITIONAL_TYPE_NAMES = ["Bool","Unit"]) and type-checks.
// @note: The real gap is at the CLI: mycelium-cli calls Interpreter::eval(), which refuses any
// @note: CoreValue::Data with EvalError::DataResult. eval_core() would accept it but is never
// @note: called by the CLI. So this is a mycelium-cli gap, NOT a language gap.
// @note: This probe should DRIFT to run=0 the day the CLI calls eval_core — that drift is the fix landing.
nodule probe;

fn main() => Unit = Unit;
